Changes
=======

v4.0.1 28 Apr 2026
  * `WithWhitelist(nil)` now records a sticky error on the Client / Cache
    rather than silently degrading to the default permissive whitelist.
    `Client.Fetch` returns this error on every call, so a misconfigured
    fetcher fails closed instead of fetching arbitrary URLs.
  * Apply the 5-hop redirect cap even when the caller supplies a custom
    `CheckRedirect` via `WithHTTPClient`. Previously a custom hook could
    suppress the cap entirely.
  * Document `Cache`'s redirect trust model: 3xx targets are followed
    subject only to the underlying http.Client policy (host trust, not
    URL trust). See package and `Cache` godoc.

v4.0.0 19 Apr 2026
  * First stable v4 release. Tracks github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v4 v4.0.0.
  * Client.Fetch now returns typed errors for non-whitelist failures:
    HTTPStatusError, BodyTooLargeError, TransportError, ParseError.
    Callers can branch retry/alert policy with errors.Is / errors.As
    instead of matching on error message strings. The underlying
    stdlib / jwk errors remain reachable via Unwrap.

v4.0.0-alpha2 13 Apr 2026
  * Compatibility release for jwx/v4 v4.0.0-scratch.15. No code changes.
  * Doc fix: package example now shows side-effect import.

v4.0.0-alpha1 8 Apr 2026
  * Initial version, extracted from github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v4/jwk.
